%% lnmarginfix.sty: a modified copy of marginfix.sty v1.2 (2020/05/06,
%% https://ctan.org/pkg/marginfix) for the lnotes class.
%% marginfix collects the \marginpar notes of a page and lays them out
%% when the page is built (\@combinefloats): a note that would run below
%% the text block is moved up into free space above it, and notes that
%% still do not fit are carried to the top of the next page.
%%
%% Changed from marginfix.sty (each change is marked "lnotes:"):
%%  1. First aid.  The LaTeX kernel repairs marginfix for its new output
%%     routine (\let\@outputbox@attachfloats\@combinefloats, in
%%     firstaid/latex2e-first-aid-for-external-files.ltx), keyed on the
%%     file name marginfix.sty, so this copy applies it itself.
%%  2. Note positions.  marginfix records the natural height of the page
%%     at the anchor.  On a \flushbottom page the body is stretched to the
%%     text height afterwards, so notes drifted above their anchors, more
%%     so further down the page; and when the page builder later broke
%%     the page before the anchor line (widow and club control, a box that
%%     did not fit), the note stayed at the bottom of the page before.
%%     This copy puts a LuaTeX user whatsit (no size, not a breakpoint)
%%     after the anchor line and, when the page is built, finds it in the
%%     column set to its final height (with its floats): the note's first
%%     baseline is aligned with the anchor's baseline (the kernel puts the
%%     top of the note box there, so a note starting with a color whatsit
%%     sat one line ascent low), and a note whose anchor is not on the page
%%     is carried to the page where it is.  \marginposadjustment still
%%     shifts every note (positive: down).  Needs LuaTeX.
%%  3. A note carried to the top of a page has its first baseline at
%%     \topskip (marginfix used \ht of the note box, which is zero when
%%     the note starts with a color or other whatsit).
%%  4. Body layout as with the kernel.  The kernel's \@addmarginpar leaves
%%     a kern and two empty boxes in the main vertical list after the
%%     anchor; marginfix leaves nothing, and some pages then broke
%%     differently (lnotes en A5: a definition moved to the previous
%%     page).  This copy leaves the same nodes.  And marginfix rewrapped
%%     the column box without the \maxdepth limit on its depth, which the
%%     kernel's \@make@normalcolbox backs up by, so a page whose last line
%%     is deep (a display, a box) was set with different glue.  With both,
%%     the body is set exactly as without marginfix.
%%  5. Warnings.  A note pushed below its anchor by the notes above it
%%     gets the kernel's "Marginpar on page N moved" (the lnotes log
%%     checkers count it); a note carried to the next page for lack of
%%     room gets "Marginpar on page N carried over to the next page".
%%  6. \ProvidesPackage name and this header.
%%
